## Worktree and commits

- Edit only in `{{ worktree }}`{% if worktree != repo %}, your own branch of the checkout `{{ repo }}`{% endif %}. Everything else is read-only, except the files your task names.
- Commit as you go: `git -C {{ worktree }} add <path>...`, then `git -C {{ worktree }} commit -s -m <message>`. Only commits are integrated: uncommitted work, or a source file left untracked (a scratch script too), fails the task.
- Refused at landing: no sign-off, `Co-authored-by`, an added symlink (the build guide's install symlinks stay in the build), `.mcp.json` or `.claude/`, the run's workspace, a judge path. Never `git push`; rebase only when this message asks.
{% endif %}- The flow running this task is the package at `{{ package }}`. An `agent-flow/` directory in a checkout is another copy, which may differ: read the running one.
