## Shared code

Code outside `{{ target }}` and its tests may change when the target needs it.

- One commit per shared change, with no target file in it; its message says why.
- Make it general: no branch on this model. State in your receipt that other models were not retested.
- After a C++/CUDA change, rebuild and install as `{{ build_guide }}` says, then check which library the interpreter loads: relinking alone leaves the installed copy stale.
{% endif %}
## Notes file

Read `{{ notes }}` first, if it exists. Read it again before you write your receipt. It never permits changing an anchor, a tolerance or a check.

## Engines and long commands
{% if gate %}
- Run model-level checks with the gate. It holds the run's device lock, starts and stops the deployment's servers itself, and its verdict line names the directory of their files:

      {{ gate }}

- One engine at a time: wait until one has exited before you start the next, and never leave one in the background.
{% endif %}- A tool call over about 8 minutes is cut while its job runs on: send a long command's output to a log file and poll every few minutes.
- Nothing wakes an ended turn. While a job you need is running, keep polling; end your turn only after its result is in and your receipt is written.
